WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.140
A Christmas party?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.080
Yes.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.920
I wanted to have fun with everyone.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.880
I thought we could have it at my place.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.730
Good morning.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.570
Good mo- Youko?!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:19.180
Huh?

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:19.890
What?

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:20.730
Hey, everyone!

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.420
Youko's clothes!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.900
She's wearing clothes!

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.990
Don't act like I don't usually wear them!

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.570
It's winter.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.740
Even Youko tries to keep out the cold.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.790
But it's true that she doesn't often wear heavy clothing.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:36.380
In elementary school, she wore shorts even in winter.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.500
I'm not wearing shorts...

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.630
Speaking from experience, you can get used to the cold.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.130
If you don't get cold easily, you won't catch colds even in winter.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.370
Really?

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.430
It sounds convincing coming from you, since you're always healthy.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.780
That's amazing.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.520
I want to become stronger, too.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.600
I don't need a coat!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.280
Don't, Alice!

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.160
Youko's just an idiot!

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.980
Hey!

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.660
I'm so excited for Christmas!

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.000
Christmas in Japan is pretty unique.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.670
What's Christmas like in England?

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.170
In my house, we go to church every
year and spend it together as a family.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.920
England's Christmas is kind of like Japan's New Year's.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.930
Lots of people in Japan seem to think it's a holiday for couples.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.770
It was originally to celebrate Jesus Christ's birth...

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:03.900
Er...

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.940
Sorry for making light of it.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.070
Merry Christmas!

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.270
What's wrong, everyone?

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.410
It's almost Christmas.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.690
You should be more festive!

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:29.070
Maybe you're more Japanese than English, after all.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:32.470
Both Japanese and English people get excited at Christmas.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.300
But the most festive person of all is...

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.180
Santa Claus!

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.510
He's even got a red outfit.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.270
So do you!

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.020
Shino, do you like Christmas?

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.650
Yes, very much so.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.900
I love spending it with everyone.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.400
I'm especially happy that I get to spend it with you this year.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.030
Shino...

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.580
A Japanese Christmas is a day to spend with Shino!

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.410
How wonderful!

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.630
Christmas is all about presents.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.930
I already asked for mine.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.930
What did you ask for?

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.060
I have a feeling it's something way out there.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:26.520
It could only be...

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.310
...love, of course.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.000
<i>She surpassed...</i>

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.370
<i>...our expectations.</i>

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:38.430
I think you already receive plenty of love.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.700
No, I'm asking for more of a "hyper love".

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.230
Why are you making such an unreasonable demand?!

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.980
In England, they say love falls with the snow.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:52.560
What?

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.460
Really?!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.220
I've never seen that happen!

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.270
Hey, Local!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.470
She's kidding, she's kidding!

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.250
How wonderful.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.970
This is far more romantic than an increased allowance.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.410
I want love for Christmas this year, too!

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.320
Yes!

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.760
What is this?

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.570
Sensei, are you spending Christmas with your boyfriend?

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:21.370
What?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.500
For me, Christmas is a day of prayer.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.250
<i>Sensei is amazing...</i>

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.860
<i>She's going to attend Mass.</i>

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:36.630
How very English.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:38.170
It's so cold.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:39.760
Maybe it's because I'm only wearing a tracksuit.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:49.060
Alice.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.980
Wait, Shino!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:19.380
This area is famous for its Christmas decorations.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.090
Aren't they beautiful?

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.520
Amazing.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.470
It's like a wonderland.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.210
Puns are difficult.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.870
Will you explain them to me?

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:52.460
Well, let's see...

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.210
Karen found a pretty flower,

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.880
and this flower doesn't wilt.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.080
Like that?

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:02.300
Huh?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.660
What does that mean?

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.430
Could you say it again?

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.930
Puns aren't supposed to mean anything...

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:20.630
Amazing.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.360
You really worked hard.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.780
It's beautiful.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.160
Welcome.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:30.200
Isa-nee, you're a model. Why aren't you wearing a Santa costume?

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.790
That has nothing to do with being a model.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.580
Youko-chan, look at me.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.880
Lookie, lookie.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.130
I'm used to seeing you in weird clothes.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.670
Aya'd look great in one, but she refuses to wear it.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.090
Karen's dressed up like Santa, too.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.830
Merry Christmas!

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.460
I already saw that.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.430
Aya, what's wrong?

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:05.150
Alice, are you calling England?

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.030
Yes.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:10.370
They actually asked me if I could come home for Christmas.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.550
What?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.540
Shouldn't you have gone?

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:17.130
But the rule of a Japanese Christmas is to spend it with you.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.420
There's no rule like that...

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:25.800
I'm so happy I got to experience a Japanese Christmas this year.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:28.800
Alice...

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.720
Oh, yeah...

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.170
I wonder if it will snow.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.480
It's still a little early.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.990
But I'm sure love is falling.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.120
It's cold.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:57.080
Later.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.120
Take care.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.480
Thank you.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.780
I had fun.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.380
So did I.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.960
Have a wonderful Holy Night.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.970
Thanks for having us.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.220
I'm having a party with my family after this.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.220
We might have one, too.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.230
Celebrating with your family sounds so English.

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:21.860
Spending a romantic Christmas with the person you love is so old-fashioned.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:24.110
Aya, is that what you'd prefer?

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:25.010
What?

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.110
I can't even imagine it.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.500
You'll have to wait until tomorrow for your present.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.130
Aww...

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.110
Shino, can we open them yet?

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:07.030
Alice, it's still dark out.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.160
It's finally present time.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.080
It's so cute.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.840
Shino, what is this?

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.360
It's a rock I picked up in England.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.590
It's my greatest treasure.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:36.660
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.140
<i>I don't want it.</i>

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.940
<i>But it's a present from Shino...</i>

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.440
T-Thanks...

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.940
Alice.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:48.590
Want these photos of Shinobu in her costume from yesterday?

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:49.740
Yes, please!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.700
Isami, thank you!

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.990
Huh?

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.760
Thank you for that wonderful song.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.310
Next up is Team White with an opening theme from a drama.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.310
You've been listening to that non-stop, Alice.

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:23.980
Yeah.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.860
Listening to the New Year's Eve bells in person is so moving.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:30.900
It's almost the new year.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.990
What was that scream?!

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.750
What happened here?

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.250
Alice, what's wrong?

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.000
I had... a nightmare...

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.610
A dream?

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.970
Oh, come on.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.550
Don't scare me like that.

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:15.110
Do you remember your first dream of the new year?

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.120
I always forget as soon as I wake up.

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:19.870
You were in mine.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:21.240
Really?

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:25.120
You appear in my dreams a lot.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.630
What's wrong?

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.790
You seem down.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.590
You always look more beautiful in my dreams.

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.550
You should be grateful.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.280
That's probably not me...

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.680
Happy New Year!

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.680
Ta-da!

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:44.980
You can't wear a kimono to school, Karen.

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:46.880
I'm surprised no one caught you.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.690
I'll change later.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:52.690
Speaking of first dreams, I had one, too.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:55.240
Something terrible happened to Alice in my dream...

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.910
Good morning... everyone.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.190
What's wrong, Shino?

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.870
You seem down.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:11.880
The truth is, Alice... Alice...

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.380
Huh?

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:16.380
Good morning.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:19.050
What's wrong, Alice?

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.710
You're dressed in English fashion today.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.260
Your uniform is different, too.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:26.020
D-Did my dream come true?!

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.980
In my dream,

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:32.090
Alice lost her memory and forgot how to speak Japanese!

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.780
Seriously?!

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.560
But she just responded to Japanese.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.820
You're just teasing us, aren't you?

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.600
I can't believe I'd experience a language barrier here...

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.980
Alice, did you really forget how to speak Japanese?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.100
Call me Youko!

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:16.730
I think it's probably because she had a nightmare for her first dream.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:19.630
Even though Alice loves Japan,

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.780
she seemed really deflated on New Year's Day.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:26.660
<i>Alice, how many pieces of mochi would you like in your ozoni?</i>

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.290
<i>Two.</i>

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:35.920
<i>Shino!</i>

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:37.380
<i>Be careful!</i>

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:39.920
<i>Mochi sticks in your throat!</i>

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.800
That was in Japanese!

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.660
You're just teasing us, aren't you?

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.810
N-No!

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:52.270
Maybe she's testing how much your English has improved.

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:54.860
It doesn't seem like it.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:00.570
I <i>do</i> love Alice when she wears cute clothes,

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:02.780
but I can't talk to her like this.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.870
I'm being tested!

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:09.040
I'm really being tested!

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:47.830
<i>Is "hello" not enough to have a conversation?!</i>

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.310
That's nothing new...

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:53.080
Karen, you can understand Alice, can't you?

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.570
Okay, come on.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:56.580
Leave it to me.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.590
Let me help, too.

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.850
I see.

00:16:13.850 --> 00:16:16.270
What did Alice say?

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:17.100
Yes.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.480
This is your fault, Shino.

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:20.480
What?!

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:21.650
Indeed.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:22.650
Why?!

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.650
Cheating is very bad.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:26.530
I know.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:30.530
I don't remember doing anything like that.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.040
Sensei, please tell me the answer.

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.370
What?

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.040
I'm a teacher. I don't think I can do that.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.580
But...

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:45.170
Shino, this must be a trial that has been imposed on you.

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.090
A trial?

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.600
I understand!

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.970
I will do my best to translate!

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.310
That's the spirit!

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:08.950
I don't understand any of it.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:14.450
Alice, do you not like me anymore?

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.540
I like you!

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.370
Oh, I heard that one.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.380
I'm sorry, Shino.

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:26.850
I was the one who thought you didn't like me anymore.

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:33.250
<i>You shouldn't step on the threshold.</i>

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.770
<i>Really?</i>

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.970
<i>You know everything, don't you?</i>

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:47.530
<i>I realised I had become more Japanese than
even Japanese people since coming to Japan.</i>

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:54.120
<i>And then, the incident occurred...</i>

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.290
<i>What's with this narration?</i>

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.370
<i>I look forward to another year with you, Shino.</i>

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:00.310
<i>Yes.</i>

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:02.130
<i>By the way, Alice...</i>

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:06.210
<i>You've grown too Japanese. I'm sick of it.</i>

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:11.840
<i>I'm into a different British girl now.</i>

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:16.060
It was such a terrible omen to start the new year with...

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:22.910
As soon as I woke up, I sent a picture of a treasure boat down a river!

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:25.940
You did what?

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.990
It's to protect myself from the omen.

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.610
I understand the situation now.

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:31.590
You're amazing, Alice.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:37.700
I'll study harder so we can speak to each other in English.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.500
No matter how Japanese you become...

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.460
Even if you become a samurai...

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.710
You'll always be Alice.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.920
Shino...

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:49.470
I know it's a little late now,

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.470
but I look forward to spending this year with you, too.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:54.970
So do I.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:56.970
Good for you two.

00:18:57.310 --> 00:19:01.300
If you become Japanese, you can become a samurai?

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:06.030
I will become more Japanese.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.150
Karen, you're already pretty Japanese.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.100
What?

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.470
Really?

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:14.320
But the way I speak...

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.660
Can't you speak normally by now?

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.580
It's difficult.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.210
It's a habit.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:25.520
You know how Ayaya is always saying, "Youko this, Youko that"?

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:27.290
It's the same thing.

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:29.800
What are you talking about?!

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:57.070
It's a little sad, isn't it?

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.080
We've still got a long way to go, though.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:04.720
How fast time flies...

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.830
Karen, don't run.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.210
We'll all be onee-san's soon.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:11.710
What?

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:15.720
We'll be second years this spring!

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:18.160
That's right.

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.720
We're moving up a year!

00:21:57.110 --> 00:21:59.380
It's got warmer.

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:00.970
Huh?

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:02.350
Alice...

00:22:02.350 --> 00:22:04.240
She fell asleep.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:14.090
Good morning, Mum.

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:15.500
Good morning, Shino.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:18.880
Good morning.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:20.880
Good morning, Dad.

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.140
What are you talking about, Shino?

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:26.300
Your father disappeared three years ago.

00:22:26.300 --> 00:22:27.720
Right, Grandpa?

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:28.890
Harsh!

00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:32.900
No, I'm not...

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:36.980
That makes me Shino's little sister, right?

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:38.900
Alice, good morning.

00:22:39.570 --> 00:22:40.900
It's time for breakfast.

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:41.910
Hooray!

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:43.320
Here.

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:46.910
This is too much!

00:22:47.950 --> 00:22:49.660
Good morning, family.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:53.130
Oh, you're up late.

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:54.920
What a huge daughter.

00:22:55.790 --> 00:23:00.970
Hey, Onee-sama... I achieved a perfect score on my most recent test.

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:03.260
Wow, that's amazing.

00:23:04.430 --> 00:23:06.010
Shino.

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:10.270
Later, Alice. You're in the way.

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.800
You're awake.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:20.440
<i>Turns out it was a dream.</i>

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:23.290
What colour is love?

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:23.820
Red.

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:24.460
Pink!

00:23:24.460 --> 00:23:25.830
The colour of hearts.

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:27.410
You're all wrong.

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:30.300
I can see the colour of Alice's heart.

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:32.230
It's a beautiful golden colour!

00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:33.590
It must be hard as a rock!

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:34.430
Ready, and...

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:35.990
See you next time!
